WHAT CHANGED SINCE ATTEMPT 4 (the actual scope of this verdict)
whatif-rate-assumptions.js's updateInvestmentReturnDisplay, val===0
branch: was `calculateExpectedReturnFromAllocation().toFixed(1)` (client
recompute), now reads `display.dataset.expectedReturn` — the server's own
%.1f figure, baked into both templates (rate-assumptions.html in-card and
quick-adjust.html QA mirror) as `data-expected-return="{{printf "%.1f"
.Settings.GetExpectedReturnFromAllocation}}"`. Also: the val!=0 "Fixed X%"
branch's roundHalfEvenDecimalString call now matches Go's raw `%.1f`
sign-preservation for negative inputs (including a rounded-to-zero
negative, e.g. -0.03 -> "-0.0") rather than dropping the sign. Confirmed
Go itself does this (`fmt.Sprintf("%.1f", -0.03)` -> "-0.0"); every
percent1 slider in the template (inflation_rate, spending_decline_rate,
phase multipliers, investment_return) has min=0, so this branch is not
keyboard-reachable in the current UI — OBSERVATION only, not a defect
(nothing on screen can show it). handlers_rates.go's roundToSignificantDigits
(server-side COLA-save rounding) has no accessible-text surface.

